EXT. LIFEBOAT, OPEN OCEAN - DAY

A white fiberglass lifeboat riding gentle swells under a vast blue sky. No land. No ships. A flare gun, a water jug, a canvas awning rolled back. The sun hammers the thwarts.

TEODORA ABELARD-NKOSI (30s, sun-scorched, a torn orange life vest, lips split) sits in the stern with an emergency radio in her lap. She stares at it. Nothing else moves for a long time.

She turns the dial. Static. Turns it back. Static. She sets it on the thwart, picks up the water jug, shakes it. Almost empty. She sets it down.

The radio gives a click.

TEODORA
(hoarse)
Hello?

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
(faint, through hiss)
...aboard, if you can hear this...

TEODORA
(grabbing the radio)
I hear you! I can hear you!

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
...say again. This is the Ocean Warden...

TEODORA
I'm in a lifeboat! Position unknown!

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Ma'am, stay calm. What is your name?

TEODORA
Teodora. Teodora Abelard-Nkosi.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Teodora, I'm Captain Ruiz-Delacroix. How many aboard?

TEODORA
One.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
One person?

TEODORA
(a beat)
Just me.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Understood. Do you have water?

TEODORA
A mouthful.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Food?

TEODORA
None.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Can you see the sun?

TEODORA
It's right above me.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Good. Teodora, listen carefully. We're picking up your signal. We're three hours out. Stay on the radio.

TEODORA
Three hours.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Three hours. Can you hold on?

TEODORA
I've held on four days.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Then three hours is easy.

She laughs, a dry broken sound, and presses the radio against her forehead. Tears cut through the salt on her cheeks.

TEODORA
It's not easy.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
No. It isn't.

TEODORA
Captain, can you just talk to me? Anything.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
What would you like to hear?

TEODORA
Anything. The weather. The news.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Weather's fine. Seas are calm. There's a bit of high cloud to the west.

TEODORA
That's nice.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
The news, honestly, isn't. But I can tell you about my dog.

TEODORA
Tell me about your dog.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
His name is Barnacle. He's a collie. He hates the ocean.

TEODORA
(laughing)
He hates the ocean?

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
He's afraid of the waves. Barks at each one.

TEODORA
Does it help?

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Not at all. But he's very committed.

Teodora closes her eyes and lets her head rest against the gunwale. The radio hisses and the swell lifts the boat and sets it down.

TEODORA
Captain?

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
Still here.

TEODORA
Keep talking.

RADIO VOICE (V.O.)
All right. Barnacle also eats socks.

She smiles, eyes shut. The sun climbs. The lifeboat rises on the swell and the radio hums on, a thin voice in the huge blue silence, and far off on the horizon something white begins to grow.
